18. Implementation roadmap
Design consolidation — wannan takarda; babu live changes.
Business contract decisions — pricing, currency/payment, quote, refunds, SLA/revisions, roles, bank verification.
Read-only re-audit — current SHAs, API URL/config, Admin auth primitives, DB schema/ACLs, deployed assets.
Branch-only implementation — dedicated API, migration files, User Side, Admin module, tests and rollback plan.
Isolated QA — synthetic data, mock bank evidence, supported Pi sandbox/test flow, authorization-negative tests and network isolation.
Patch review — complete changed-file list/diff, SQL migration, tests, unresolved decisions; Mainnet only after explicit approval.
Controlled go-live — official Pi requirements, terms/pricing, verified bank destination if used, security review and QA sign-off.
19. Non-negotiable change controls
No SQL write, Storage mutation, GitHub commit, deployment or real payment without explicit approval.
Before replacing an existing file, state the exact path/name so the owner can save a copy; provide the complete replacement, not snippets.
Do not modify ALBUKHR Dock Navigation.
Do not change environment-core.js, supabase-core.js, page-auth-guard.js or shared pi-auth-core.js as part of this service unless a separate reviewed patch proves necessity.
Do not reuse External Projects tables/permissions/bucket for dApp service.
Do not reuse Core Project liquidity validation or A2U payout as service checkout.
Keep gateway/payment channels disabled until DB, auth, API contract, tests and approval are complete.
record_pi_login/security issue is parked, not resolved; do not modify it during this work without returning to it with explicit authorization.
